# Campamento Pokémon — Task Checklist

## Phase 1: Planning & Architecture
- [/] Create implementation plan with architecture decisions
- [ ] Get user approval on plan

## Phase 2: Project Initialization
- [ ] Run `npx create-vite@latest` for the project
- [ ] Install dependencies: react-router-dom, zustand, react-hook-form, clsx, tailwind-merge, firebase
- [ ] Configure Tailwind CSS with custom breakpoints (1920px, 990px, 767px, 510px, 480px)
- [ ] Configure Vite for GitHub Pages deployment (base path)

## Phase 3: Project Structure
- [ ] Create folder structure: /pages, /components, /services, /store, /hooks, /utils
- [ ] Set up React Router with all route placeholders
- [ ] Create empty page components (Login, Pokedex, Team, Shop, AdminDashboard)

## Phase 4: Services & Store (Firebase + API)
- [ ] Configure Firebase (Authentication + Firestore) in /services/firebase.js
- [ ] Create auth service (login, register, role detection)
- [ ] Create Firestore service (teams CRUD, store catalog CRUD)
- [ ] Create PokéAPI service (fetch Pokémon, fetch items)
- [ ] Set up Zustand store (auth state, team state, shop state)

## Phase 5: UI Components
- [ ] Layout components (Navbar, ProtectedRoute, RoleGuard)
- [ ] Shared UI components (Button, Card, Modal, Loader, Badge)
- [ ] Login page UI + react-hook-form
- [ ] Pokédex page (search, grid, pagination)
- [ ] Team Builder page (drag/add Pokémon, save team)
- [ ] Shop page (list items, buy/assign)
- [ ] Admin Dashboard (add/edit/delete items)

## Phase 6: Verification
- [ ] Test responsive breakpoints
- [ ] Test auth flow (user vs admin roles)
- [ ] Test PokéAPI fetching
- [ ] Test Firestore CRUD operations
- [ ] Build and verify GitHub Pages config
